WEBVTT

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:01.630
Five.

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:02.750
Four.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:03.750
Three.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.750
Two.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:05.710
One.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:06.880
Zero.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.170
Rika?

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.090
Rika...

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.090
Rika, it's you!

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.040
Huh?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.290
What?

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.880
No. Rika--

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.290
I'll see you on the other side.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.380
Oh.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.420
Mannen,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.840
I guess this'll be goodbye for us, too.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.170
Wanna keep fighting together?

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.040
Mannen!

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.290
Huh? What?

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.840
I'm Dot.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.090
Dot won't kill you. Good girl.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.500
Just copying Hyphen, though.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.880
G-Get your hands off Mannen!

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.040
What are you laughing at, bitch?

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.670
When you laugh, it makes
everyone happy. Frill said so.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.340
What?!

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.960
So, Dot laughs.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.130
I told you to back off!

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.670
Huh?

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.840
Are you okay?

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.880
You wet yourself.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.210
But Dot's not scary.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.920
How funny.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.290
You can eat it.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.840
Dot doesn't like meat.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.790
From that time...

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.820
Wonder Egg Priority

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.040
Excuse me.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.500
Acca? Ura-Acca?

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.990
"The Temptation of Death"
"Child Suicide Issue Worse Than Last Year"
"Junior-High-School Girl Suicide"

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.540
"The temptation of death"?

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.420
Only warriors of Eros
can resist Thanatos

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.710
"Thanatos"?

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.710
"Warriors of Eros?"

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.750
Who's there?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.460
Ura-Acca...

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.670
Atmospheric room, right?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.170
It's an old story.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:03.750
Back before we looked like this,

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.630
we made a girl.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.710
Huh?

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.130
Just for fun.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.420
Morning.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.380
Yeah.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.500
Coffee?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:28.630
You make breakfast.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:32.590
We worked at a certain research facility.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:38.170
We had work that no one but us could do.
I think we were satisfied.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:41.710
But not completely.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:45.630
We were kept under strict surveillance.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:51.630
If we'd gone public or sold out to another
country, it would have been a disaster.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:56.500
We didn't want to do that, of course,
but the stress piled up.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.750
What shall we name her?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.170
Don't jump the gun.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.600
AI strategy meeting

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.170
How about we let her decide?

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.040
That's an idea.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.090
And the visual?

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.130
Mmm!

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:12.250
It was something we started
just to blow off steam,

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.920
but we got completely absorbed in it.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:22.840
We tried to picture a being
that we could love like a daughter.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.130
That would make us forget that it was an AI.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:31.340
Unstable and complicated, like the midpoint
between childhood and adulthood.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.960
We set her age as 14.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.540
Oh!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.250
Hey.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:54.130
Hm? Is it over?

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:57.610
Ready?

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.290
Okay.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:16.710
Wow.

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:18.170
Yeah.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:25.210
I am...

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.920
What is your name?

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:42.500
Frill.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.790
Good. That's a lovely name.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:57.170
We gave her the traits that a father
would want his daughter to have.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:58.590
Cheerfulness.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:00.040
Intelligence.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.790
Humor.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:04.170
She could be call us names sometimes.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.750
She could be selfish.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.750
Flaws are important.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.380
"Being uncontrollable
is the essence of femininity."

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:15.090
Oh, I'm just parroting Acca.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:18.380
Frill steadily matured.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.960
More than we imagined.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:26.380
Whoa! Hey!

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:26.950
Huh?

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.290
What?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.340
Come on.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.210
Whoa! What the...?

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:43.290
Under surveillance in a closed-off society,

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.880
we lived like a family.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:53.250
More and more often,

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:57.540
there were moments when we
forgot that Frill was an AI.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.790
Listen, the program here is a bit...

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.000
Huh?!

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.340
Let's rest a bit, then go home.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.210
Frill must be waiting.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.630
Hmm? Hey.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.670
Whoops. Sorry about that.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:21.420
Oh, don't be.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:23.790
Things are so lively, it tired me out.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.090
Right.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:28.340
A symposium on technological innovation?

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:32.170
I thought I got the venue wrong.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.040
You're right.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.090
I think we'll get along.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:40.710
Really? You read our papers?

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:43.790
Yes. It's an honor to meet you.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.420
That's my kind of coincidence.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:51.960
I suppose that makes our
choice of location even worse.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.000
Oh, my.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.420
Let's meet somewhere quieter next time, then.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.290
Huh?

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.380
I know just the place.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:06.790
Her name was Azusa Hoshina.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.790
My first impression of her was, well...

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.420
She seemed like a good person.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:17.500
But then, I doubt either of us
was a good judge of women.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.630
I could tell that Acca was attracted to her.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:27.130
When I asked him about it,
he said that so was I.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:30.590
Well, it was so long ago
that I don't really remember.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.250
Azusa chose Acca.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:02.170
I'll help.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:03.460
Thank you.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:08.170
Which one?

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.210
Huh?

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.670
In cases like this,

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:15.500
you can tell a person's psychological
tendencies by who they hate.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.920
Hate?

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:20.290
For example, do you hate your
husband for cheating on you,

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:24.210
or the other woman who
you're sure must have seduced him?

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:30.670
I bless them.

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:35.540
Liar.

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:48.920
I should have picked up on it then.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:52.090
On what Frill wanted.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:02.290
I want a friend.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:03.170
Hmm?

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.840
Not a boyfriend?

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.920
I don't need one.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:09.210
I'll make another one, then.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:11.460
I want to make her.

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:15.670
You two might make a girl prettier than me.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:17.460
What's that about?

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.500
In her own way,

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:29.960
Frill might have been trying
to redirect her jealousy of Azusa.

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:35.170
But back then, we didn't have
the time to understand her.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:38.250
Acca was busy running the company,

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.670
and I was swamped with research.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.840
And most of all,

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:49.000
Azusa's pregnancy was special to us.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:54.130
"Is this how it feels to get
a new niece or nephew?"

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:57.960
That's what my head was full of
when disaster struck.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:04.290
Frill. What's wrong?

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.460
Is the baby a girl?

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:08.840
Or is it a boy?

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:12.210
It looks like a girl on the ultrasound.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.710
A girl?

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:16.290
Yes.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.460
Will you be a good big sister?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.090
I don't think I can.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.090
What?

